<PageLayout title="Privacy information">
<main id="main" class="legal-main">
<p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY INFORMATION</p>
<h1>What happens to your information.</h1>
<p>Last updated September 27, 2026.</p>
<p>I’m Jaylan, and I operate <Wordmark inline/> personally in Tennessee. This notice describes the current public website and its browser-prepared request forms.</p>
<h2>What you enter in a form</h2>
<p>The project, support, and consultation forms ask for your name, email address, and a description of what you need. Depending on the form, you can also provide a business or project name, service choice, budget range, timing, issue category and impact, website or service involved, or preferred consultation date, time, and time zone. These details help describe your request.</p>
<p>The forms prepare a request in your browser. They do not submit it to a server or automatically send an email. You can copy the request, open a prefilled Gmail compose page, pass it to your device’s email app, or download it as a text file. You review and send it yourself.</p>
<p>Do not include passwords, recovery codes, payment-card details, Social Security numbers, or confidential client files. Ask me about an appropriate way to share private materials before sending them.</p>
<h2>If you choose to email me</h2>
<p>You can contact me at <a href="mailto:tkjet718@gmail.com">tkjet718@gmail.com</a>. If you send a message, I receive your email address, the message, and any other information you include so I can respond to your request.</p>
<p>Your email provider and my provider, Google’s Gmail, handle the message. Opening Gmail takes you to Google and prefills the request in its compose page; the message is not sent until you choose to send it. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a> for its practices. The website cannot confirm delivery, delete messages from your email account, or control how email providers retain their copies. An email, copied request, or downloaded draft is separate from the form on this page.</p>
<h2>What stays on your device</h2>
<p>Your ambience preference can be saved in your browser until you clear this site’s stored data. It is used to remember whether you paused the background. The website does not use cookies.</p>
<p>The site keeps form drafts and sample shopping-bag contents only while the page is open; it does not save them to its own database or browser storage. Your browser may separately remember or restore form fields through autofill or session recovery. Downloaded drafts remain wherever you save them until you remove them.</p>
<h2>Tracking and third-party content</h2>
<p>The public website is delivered through Sites at a <code>chatgpt.site</code> address. The hosting service receives the network and request information needed to deliver and protect the site, such as the requested page, time, browser information, and network address. The site itself does not add a visitor account or analytics profile.</p>
<p>Fonts, images, and scripts load from this site. No third-party analytics, advertising scripts, tracking pixels, payment forms, or social-media embeds are installed. The sample websites are hosted here too.</p>
<p>This preview does not perform cross-site tracking, transmit information to advertising platforms, or read browser Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signals. Following an external link takes you to a separate website whose privacy practices apply there.</p>
<h2>Questions about your information</h2>
<p><a href="mailto:tkjet718@gmail.com?subject=Privacy%20request">Email me with a privacy question or request</a>, including a request to review, correct, or delete information you previously sent me. Describe your request without sending passwords or identity documents. There is no client account or automated data-request portal on this site.</p>
<h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
<p>Updates will appear on this page with a revised date. This notice will need to reflect the actual providers and data handling when automatic form delivery or other new services are connected.</p>
</main>
</PageLayout>
